# CALLER-BASELINE -- the vendored QuickJS's ACTUAL Function.prototype.caller
# behaviour, recorded 2026-08-30 by tests/fixtures/crashfix/caller_probe.c
# (gated by make test-crashfix-caller).
#
# GAP CLOSED 2026-09-02. The paragraph below is the ORIGINAL one, kept beside
# the correction per this tree's rule (AGENTS.md #1: "where that happened the
# correction is kept beside the old claim ... because somebody is going to
# arrive holding the old sentence"), followed by what changed and how it was
# verified.
#
# ---- ORIGINAL (2026-08-30), describing the gap this file used to record ----
# THIS FILE RECORDS THE GAP, NOT THE GOAL. Every browser answers
#   called_by_fn = "function"   (a non-strict fn's .caller is its caller)
#   walk         = "null-at-top" (the frame chain ends in null)
# and the kimi specimen (trustdecision fm.js, "caller of undefined") walks
# .caller expecting exactly that: it calls fn.caller.caller... and dies with
# "cannot read property 'caller' of undefined" on the FIRST hop, because this
# engine answers undefined where a browser answers the function object. See
# third_party/quickjs/quickjs.c:14993 js_function_proto_caller, which returns
# JS_UNDEFINED unconditionally for non-strict functions.
#
# The fix belongs to third_party/quickjs (not the crashfix agent's tree); the
# patch is written out in the crashfix wave-1 report.
# ---- END ORIGINAL -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# WHAT CHANGED: js_function_proto_caller (quickjs.c:14993) now walks
# ctx->rt->current_stack_frame looking for the frame matching this_val by the
# same object-identity rule js_build_backtrace uses (:6753-6766), and returns
# that frame's prev_frame->cur_func -- the real calling function -- instead of
# JS_UNDEFINED. .arguments was split onto its own getter
# (js_function_proto_arguments) so it keeps the old JS_UNDEFINED-always
# behaviour; sharing one getter would have made `.arguments` start returning
# a function object too (the trap named in the wave-1 report).
#
# called_by_fn is now "function" (a caller found on the live frame chain is
# returned, dup'd). walk is now "null-at-top": the chain terminates cleanly
# instead of exposing QuickJS's internal top-level-program pseudo-function
# (JS_EvalFunctionInternal runs the whole script as an ordinary call, so an
# IIFE's immediate caller is otherwise that internal frame) -- caught by
# actually running this probe: the first patch draft (no eligibility check on
# the found caller) printed `"walk":"THROW:invalid property access"` here,
# because reading .caller a second hop on that pseudo-function then hit the
# pre-existing has_prototype gate (top-level/eval/module code is parsed
# without JS_PARSE_FUNC_STATEMENT/VAR/EXPR and so never gets has_prototype
# set, quickjs.c:34763). See the SECOND TRAP paragraph on
# js_function_proto_caller's own comment for the fix (an eligibility check on
# the found caller, not just on this_val).
#
# strict stays "THREW" -- that part already matched a browser and is
# untouched.
#
# format: exactly one non-# line, the JSON the probe prints, got==want.
{"called_by_fn":"function","walk":"null-at-top","strict":"THREW"}
